                <h3 class="h3 fw-bold text-dark mt-4 mb-3">
                    Summary
                </h3>

                <div class="alert alert-primary border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">

                    <ul class="mb-0">

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            A constructor is used to initialize an object.
                        </li>

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            A constructor has the same name as its class.
                        </li>

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            A constructor does not have a return type.
                        </li>

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            A constructor is called when an object is created.
                        </li>

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            Constructors can be parameterless or parameterized.
                        </li>

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            A class can contain multiple overloaded constructors.
                        </li>

                        <li class="mb-2">
                            The <b>this</b> keyword can refer to the current object
                            and can also participate in constructor chaining.
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            Constructors are widely used in professional C#
                            and ASP.NET Core applications.
                        </li>

                    </ul>

